  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{-4x+12}{3x-9}?$",
  "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4x+12}{3x-9} & =\\frac{-4(x-3)}{3(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\cancel{(x-3)}}{3\\cancel{(x-3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
